From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd/virgl: the WDDM 2.1 DDI and NV12 textures shared between devices

The D3D11 runtime offers NV12 textures shared across devices and processes (D3D11_OPTIONS4's
ExtendedNV12SharedTextureSupported) only to drivers on the WDDM 2.1 DDI (d3d11.dll's CheckFeatureSupport reads the
negotiated DDI version: >= 5). The UMD offers D3DWDDM2_1_DDI_SUPPORTED after 2.0: 2.0's device table with the sync
token entries (AcquireResource/ReleaseResource: nothing to do) and DXGI 1.5's base table with OfferResources1 and
ReclaimResources1 (nothing offered, everything reclaimed OK); the video table asked for with it (sub-ID 5,
D3DWDDM2_1DDI_VIDEO_FUNCTIONS: 2.0's and HDR metadata, unused) - without it no D3D11 video device was made.
WINBOAT_D3D_WDDM2=0 leaves both WDDM 2 DDIs out.

And the sharing itself: a shared NV12/P010 texture (one slice, not decoder output) makes its luma plane with
PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_CHROMA_PLANE, which the winsys passes to the kernel driver (VIRGL_RESOURCE_FLAG_CHROMA_PLANE =
its VIOGPU_RESOURCE_FLAG_CHROMA_PLANE): that allocation - the runtime resource's - also makes the chroma plane. Both
the maker and whoever opens it import the chroma plane from the allocation (winsys: a D3DKMT_ALLOC handle with
plane 1, VIOGPU_RES_INFO's ChromaId), and OpenResource rebuilds the NV12/P010 surface from the two planes.
dx-test: "NV12 textures shared between devices" (legacy and NT handles).
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h
index 3b348e6..5447592 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h
@@ -175,6 +175,9 @@ static inline unsigned pipe_to_virgl_flags(const struct virgl_screen *vs,
    if (pflags & PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_MAP_COHERENT)
       out_flags |= VIRGL_RESOURCE_FLAG_MAP_COHERENT;
 
+   if (pflags & PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_CHROMA_PLANE)
+      out_flags |= VIRGL_RESOURCE_FLAG_CHROMA_PLANE;
+
    return out_flags;
 }
 
